  "body": "As described in https://github.com/w3c/editing/issues/256, `document.execCommand(\"indent\")` has been generating `<ul>` right inside `<ul>` (or `<ol>` right inside `<ol>`), causing a conflict with [their content models](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-ul-element).\r\n\r\nI guess we have two options:\r\n\r\n* Change the API behavior. This needs implementer interests.\r\n* Change the content model. Every browser supports lists inside a list, so maybe a simpler option?\r\n* Or, do nothing and deal with the conflict. A note should still be helpful in this case.",
